    "created_at": "2026-05-18T16:22:38Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-05-18T16:22:38Z",
    "body": "> The performance cost during parsing could be pretty bad if the cloning of all selected options (seen so far) happens for every `option` end tag, right?\r\n\r\nAgreed, thanks for catching that! I pushed a change to stop updating selectedcontent elements during option parsing if the select is multiple, and instead update them at the end of the select tag's parsing.",
