    "created_at": "2026-07-24T17:54:41Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-07-24T17:54:41Z",
    "body": "> Is it intentional that #selectedness-setting-algorithm [bails](https://whatpr.org/html/12430/56ec622...4bb6f73/form-elements.html#selectedness-setting-algorithm:~:text=If%20element%20%27s%20has%20the%20multiple%20attribute%20is%20absent%2C%20and%20attribute%2C%20then%20return%2E) for select multiple?\r\n\r\nYes, because we don't want to deselect other options in response to an option's selectedness being changed in a `<select multiple>`, because its fine for zero or many options to be selected.\r\n\r\n> Wouldn't this imply that selecting an <option> by script (which goes through [#ask-for-a-reset](https://whatpr.org/html/12430/56ec622...4bb6f73/form-elements.html#:~:text=ask%20for%20a%20reset,-given%20this)) is broken?\r\n\r\nGood catch, yeah I agree that is broken. Sounds like we should make \"ask for a reset\" update selectedcontent elements if the select has the multiple attribute? Do you think this would work?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
