    "body": "> The performance cost during parsing could be pretty bad if the cloning of all selected options (seen so far) happens for every `option` end tag, right?\r\n\r\nWe discussed in WHATNOT today the equivalent case but for DOM-inserted elements. Maybe check if there's a perf problem for a page with 1000 or 10,000 selected `option` elements that are inserted with `appendChild()` instead of from parsing.",
